# Tello drone agent control

When the user asks (in natural language) to fly, move, take off, land, or check the drone, **you** are the main controller. Translate their intent into bridge calls. Keep the human kill switch sacred — never disable it.

## Prerequisites

A bridge should be running in a terminal:

```bash
python tello_agent_bridge.py --auto
# or --sim if Tello Wi-Fi is unavailable
```

Base URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8765`

## How to command the drone

Prefer structured `/exec` after you resolve zones. Use `/nl` when helpful.

```bash
# status / zones
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8765/status
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8765/zones

# natural language (bridge maps common phrases)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8765/nl \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"text":"move the drone from the beginning position to area 7"}'

# explicit command (preferred once you know the zone id)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8765/exec \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"cmd":"go to ZONE_7"}'

# emergency soft stop + land in place
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8765/abort
```

Long flights: allow a long HTTP timeout (up to several minutes).

## Zone language map

| User says | Zone id |
|-----------|---------|
| beginning / start / home / hub / inizio | HUB |
| area 7 / zona 7 / zone 7 | ZONE_7 |
| north | NORTH_OPEN |
| pad | PAD |
| under mezz / mezz | UNDER_MEZZ / MEZZ_TOP |

Always `GET /zones` if unsure. Confirm the mapped command briefly, then execute.

## Safety

- On user panic ("stop", "abort", "kill"): `POST /abort` immediately.
- Do not call `emergency()` motor cut unless the user explicitly demands an instant drop.
- Prefer `--auto` / sim when Wi-Fi to the Tello is down; tell the user which backend connected.
